[{"id":"sreset-predict","itemId":"synchronous-reset","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">q_sync</code> has a synchronous reset: at a rising edge where <code class=\"nobreak\">rst_sync</code> is 1, it becomes 0; at every other rising edge, it takes <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>. Cycles 0 and 1 are drawn for you. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">q_sync</code> for the rest.","explanationHtml":"<p>At each rising edge, look at <code class=\"nobreak\">rst_sync</code> first. It is 1 at the edges that start cycles 2, 5 and 6, so <code class=\"nobreak\">q_sync</code> is 0 there, even where <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> is 1. At the other edges <code class=\"nobreak\">q_sync</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>: 1 in cycles 3 and 7, and 0 in cycle 4.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"resets-sync","source":"hdl/level-02/resets/resets_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"resets_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"rst_sync","path":"resets_tb.rst_sync","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1.5,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[4.5,"1"],[6.5,"0"]]},{"label":"d","path":"resets_tb.d","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1.5,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[5.5,"1"]]},{"label":"q_sync","path":"resets_tb.q_sync","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1,"0"],[3,"1"],[4,"0"],[7,"1"]],"samples":["1","0","0","1","0","0","0","1"]}]},"answer":"q_sync","prefill":[0,1]},{"id":"sreset-predict-mid","itemId":"synchronous-reset","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">q_sync</code> has lesson 2.3's synchronous reset. In this simulation some pulses on <code class=\"nobreak\">rst_sync</code> are short, and some begin or end in the middle of a cycle. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">q_sync</code> for every cycle.","explanationHtml":"<p>Only the value of <code class=\"nobreak\">rst_sync</code> at a rising edge counts (lesson 2.3). The short pulses in cycles 0 and 5 are over before the next edge, so <code class=\"nobreak\">q_sync</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> there: 1 in cycles 1 and 6. <code class=\"nobreak\">rst_sync</code> rises late in cycle 1 and is still 1 at the next two edges, so <code class=\"nobreak\">q_sync</code> is 0 in cycles 2 and 3, not from the moment the reset rose. The reset that rises in the middle of cycle 6 clears <code class=\"nobreak\">q_sync</code> at the edge that starts cycle 7. At every other edge <code class=\"nobreak\">q_sync</code> takes <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"resets-mid","source":"hdl/level-02/resets/resets_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"resets_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"rst_sync","path":"resets_tb.rst_sync","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[0.7,"1"],[0.9,"0"],[1.7,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[5.7,"1"],[5.9,"0"],[6.5,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"d","path":"resets_tb.d","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5.5,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"q_sync","path":"resets_tb.q_sync","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[2,"0"],[4,"1"],[5,"0"],[6,"1"],[7,"0"]],"samples":["1","1","0","0","1","0","1","0"]}]},"answer":"q_sync"},{"id":"sreset-find-bug","itemId":"synchronous-reset","role":"core","promptHtml":"This flip-flop should have a synchronous reset: <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> is looked at only at rising edges, so a short pulse on <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> between two edges changes nothing. Its testbench fails. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p><code>or posedge rst</code> in the event list makes the block run the moment <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> rises, so the reset acts at once, without the clock: that is an asynchronous reset (lesson 2.3). The testbench's first failure comes 1 ns into a 2 ns pulse between two edges, at 12 ns: <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> is already 0. Written <code>always_ff @(posedge clk) begin</code>, the block runs only at rising edges, <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> is looked at only then, and the pulse is never seen. The <code>if (rst)</code> line is right: both kinds of reset need it.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-02/sreset_bug/sreset_bug.sv","firstLine":1,"lines":[[{"text":"// A flip-flop with a synchronous reset: at a rising edge of clk where rst","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// is 1, q becomes 0, and at every other rising edge q takes d. rst is","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// looked at only at rising edges, so a pulse on rst that comes and goes","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// between two edges changes nothing.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"sreset_bug","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" rst,   ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// looked at only at rising edges","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" d,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" q","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"or","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" rst) ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"if","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" (rst) q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"1'b0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"else","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"     q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" d;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]],"bugLine":11,"fixLine":"always_ff @(posedge clk) begin"},{"id":"sreset-fill-value","itemId":"synchronous-reset","role":"core","promptHtml":"At a rising edge where <code class=\"nobreak\">rst_sync</code> is 1, <code class=\"nobreak\">q_sync</code> must become 0. Type the value the line gives it.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">1'b0</code> is one bit, set to 0 (lesson 1.3's sized numbers). The line that tests <code class=\"nobreak\">rst_sync</code> comes first in the block, so at an edge where it is 1, this value wins over <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code>.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-02/resets/resets.sv","firstLine":11,"totalLines":20,"before":["  always_ff @(posedge clk) begin"],"blankLine":{"left":"    if (rst_sync) q_sync <= ","right":";"},"after":["    else          q_sync <= d;","  end"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk) ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]],"blankLine":{"left":[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"if","color"